  "notes": "Virginia art-R&B — Neptunes-built and then Polow da Don, 1999–2006; the Neptunes' own model supplies that production lane, so what is encoded here is the artist's. The research gives \"84–99 straight (backbeat 2&4)\" with five sourced tempos, so the mode is 97. The drum claim is unusually concrete: the sourced record is \"explicitly a **Roland TR-808** record — 808 kick, 808 clap/snare on 2&4, 808 hats and cowbell, nothing acoustic; the drums are the arrangement\". So `swing.amount` is 0.50 with `offGridMs` 0 and `quantizeStrength` 0.94 — a machine, not a player — `lockTo808` is 0.6, the clap sits within a millisecond of the snare, and the perc lanes are cowbell, rim and snap. This is one of the section's true 808 models: \"808 sub-bass as the only bass voice, one or two notes per bar, long decay\", so `drums.bass808` is authored with role `bassline` and there is deliberately **no** `bassline` block, because the two cannot both sound. Harmony is \"minimal — often a single minor chord or a two-note synth motif across the whole record\", so the single-chord family carries a weight of 7 and the triad share is 0.6, the highest in this section. \"The vocal is chant-forward with a hard, unsentimental attack and near-spoken verses. Note density low, hook built by repetition\" is the staccato articulation, `twoBarCellRepeat`, a 2–4 pitch motif and a riff-dominant contour. ⚠ The research marks the key claim `[LOW-CONF]`. ⚠ Every velocity, density and portamento number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is INFERRED: the entry's Keys line gives \"minor-mode, one- or two-chord [LOW-CONF]\" and enumerates no tonic, so the values here and their weights are this author's reading of that line. ⚠ **`chords.harmonicRhythm` re-weighted (2026-08-17, harmony variety floor).** The entry gives the one-chord and the two-chord bed equal billing — \"minor-mode, one- or two-chord\" / \"often a single minor chord or a two-note synth motif across the whole record\" — and the engine's `vamp` value is *one* chord held for the whole clip (`generators::chords`: \"One chord for the whole pattern\"), so a `vamp` weight of 6-of-8 made the two-chord half of that sentence almost unreachable. `vamp` keeps the top weight; the two-chord reading is now reachable at both rates. ⚠ The split between those two rates is **INFERRED** — the entry names the device, not its rate.",
